WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:05.940
Hearings continue today for the Council’s draft Long Term Plan.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.500
And Waimakariri District Councillors say they are pleased with the amount and quality

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.320
of feedback they’re receiving from the community.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.820
We've got 60 submissions that we're listening to 
verbally over the next few days

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.620
out of over 800 that have been put in.
So it's really good to hear from people

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:28.380
firsthand of what they're thinking and
to be able to ask some questions around

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.680
that process.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.440
The verbal submissions
are very important as we see face to face

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.240
with the people that want to come
along to council and have their issues

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.760
that they wish us to listen to and that
is so important for us to hear their side

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.800
of the story and it helps us make our
decision in a way that we need to.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.910
Verbal submissions will be completed today, Councillors will then consider all the

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:56.760
feedback from the consultation process and go into deliberations from May 29th to 31st.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:00.870
Formal adoption of the LTP is expected to take place at a Council

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.960
Meeting on the 19th of June and we’ll let you know of the

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.680
key decisions made as they take place.

